From 79686b95d0c5ebc66d744f5963e7ae7540d0ff62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:27:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cpukit/microblaze: Return the TLS variable in
 __tls_get_addr()

GCC lowers every MicroBlaze thread-local storage access to a call of
__tls_get_addr().  For the general dynamic model, used for an extern
_Thread_local object, the argument points to a GOT entry pair which
the static link fills with module 1 and the offset of the object in
the TLS segment.  For the local dynamic model the offset is zero and
GCC adds the DTPREL offset of the object to the result.

__tls_get_addr() ignored its argument and returned the thread pointer,
which is the start of the TLS data on MicroBlaze (TLS variant I without
a TCB offset).  This was right only for the local dynamic model.  An
extern _Thread_local object always got the address of the first object
of the TLS segment, see sptls04.

Return the thread pointer plus the offset, as the ARM port does.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cpukit/score/cpu/microblaze/__tls_get_addr.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cpukit/score/cpu/microblaze/__tls_get_addr.c b/cpukit/score/cpu/microblaze/__tls_get_addr.c
index 97f46975e4..08ee5dc374 100644
--- a/cpukit/score/cpu/microblaze/__tls_get_addr.c
+++ b/cpukit/score/cpu/microblaze/__tls_get_addr.c
@@ -47,9 +47,15 @@ void *__tls_get_addr( const TLS_Index *ti )
 {
   const Thread_Control *executing;
 
-  (void) ti;
+  /*
+   * There is only the static thread-local storage block of the executable.
+   * The thread pointer is the start of its data, see
+   * CPU_THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE_VARIANT, and the linker resolves the offset
+   * relative to the start of the TLS segment.
+   */
+  _Assert( ti->module == 1 );
 
   executing = _Thread_Get_executing();
 
-  return executing->Registers.thread_pointer;
+  return (char *) executing->Registers.thread_pointer + ti->offset;
 }
